    "summary": "Epic Dark Star suite anchors high‑energy first set",
    "blurb": "The concert opens with a solid first set featuring Truckin', Tennessee Jed and a spirited Black Throated Wind. The second set delivers an expansive Dark Star > Me And My Uncle > Dark Star > Wharf Rat > Sugar Magnolia sequence that stands out as the highlight. A lively encore of One More Saturday Night rounds out the night.",
    "review": "April 24 1972 finds the Dead delivering a thrilling European night at Rheinhalle. The first set rolls on tight, high‑energy momentum with Truckin' and Tennessee Jed leading into a gritty Black Throated Wind that showcases Bob’s vocal grit and Jerry’s crisp guitar tone. The centerpiece is an epic Dark Star suite—Dark Star > Me And My Uncle > Dark Star > Wharf Rat > Sugar Magnolia—that glows despite the muddy audience tape; Garcia’s crystalline lead lines weave through Keith’s echo‑laden piano, creating a texture that many listeners describe as “pwns the show.” Though the recording is far from pristine, the improvisational flow and the band’s locked‑in interplay make this night a must‑hear for collectors seeking an early‑’70s European gem. The encore caps it off with a rollicking One More Saturday Night that leaves the room buzzing.",
